  "verification_method": "Per file: local md5 -> `hsi put` at the mirrored path -> md5 computed SERVER-SIDE by `hsi hashcreate` (no bytes transferred back) -> compare BOTH md5s AND the size read back from HPSS. A marker is written only on a digest match, write-to-temp + rename, so the resume guard validates COMPLETENESS not EXISTENCE (BEN-023). The manifest is built from the MARKERS, never from the loop's counters, so a crashed loop cannot claim more than was verified.",
  "TWO_INDEPENDENT_DIGEST_FAMILIES_AGREE": "md5 here (36/36 local == server-side) and sha256 from job 56760314 (36/36), computed in separate jobs by separate tools. Every size agrees across both passes and against the 13:12Z metadata walk. Agreement across two algorithms is stronger evidence than one algorithm repeated.",
  "rates": {
    "copy_MB_per_s": 161.15,
    "digest_only_MB_per_s": 223.97,
    "note": "161 MB/s for read+transfer+server-side hash against 224 MB/s for read-only. The gap is the write side and is expected; quote whichever matches the operation being estimated. The earlier 170 MB/s figure came from a single 2.68 GB read and should not be cited for either."
  },
  "NOTHING_WRITTEN_TO_THE_REPO_TREE": "Launcher, path list, markers, log and manifest all live in /pscratch/sd/j/josephrb/mnv-digest-work, OUTSIDE /pscratch/sd/j/josephrb/MINERvA-OmniFold. That tree is the object of today's inventory and is under the eight-verb no-touch list; this receipt is assembled and committed on the local side.",
  "overlap_with_prior_archive": "ZERO by enumeration. The only other bulk HPSS archive is mnv-p3f-pet-fullevent-final (240 objects, the p3f_pet_fullevent/final tree, job 56692312, 1,134,998,230,283 B) and no quoted product lives in it. So the 0.874 TB already protected did NOT reduce this ask -- it reduces the coverage gap over the whole 5.977 TB ignored set, which is a different denominator. Those two facts were adjacent in the escalation and are not the same fact.",
  "NOT_VERIFIED": [
    "That HPSS still returns these bytes after a tape migration. `hsi hashverify` against the stored hash answers that and needs no local copy. Owner: the PET lane, triggered by a dated OPEN_ITEMS entry rather than a wakerctl watch, because the waker runs on the frozen cluster tree.",
    "That the 36 are the RIGHT set. They are what VALIDATION_LEDGER.md and docs/analysis-note/*.tex name by path, and 35 of the 36 are named ONLY by the ledger -- the file with no per-row id scheme, which merge_guard.sh refuses as unattributable. The derivation is reproducible; its authority is thin.",
    "Anything about the remaining 5.65 TB of the ignored set. Step 3's disposition is still unwritten and is sequenced after review."
  ],
